<title>GERMANY: German money market closed for May 1 holiday.</title>
<headline>German money market closed for May 1 holiday.</headline>
<dateline>FRANFURT 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>- The German money market is closed on Thursday for the May 1 public holiday. Trading will resume on Friday May 2.</p>
<p>German bond markets are also closed for the holiday. The June Bund future will continue to be traded on London's LIFFE exchange.</p>
</text>
